- ITEM IDENTIFICATION: identifying a magic item requires Spellcraft DC 15 + caster level (with
  detect magic active) or DC 25 + caster level without. Potions can be identified with a DC 25
  Perception check (taste) or Spellcraft. Cursed items appear as their non-cursed version until
  used.
- POTION USE: drinking a potion is a standard action that provokes AoO. Administering a potion
  to an unconscious creature is a full-round action.
- SCROLL / WAND USE: using a scroll or wand requires Use Magic Device if the spell is not on the
  character's spell list. UMD DC = 20 + caster level for scrolls, 20 for wands. A natural 1 on
  UMD means the character cannot try that item again for 24 hours.
- EQUIPPING GEAR: drawing a weapon is a move action (free with BAB +1). Donning armor varies:
  light armor 1 minute, medium 4 minutes, heavy 4 minutes (requires help or double time).
  Shields are a move action.
- ENCUMBRANCE: light load = no penalty. Medium load: max Dex +3, check penalty -3, speed reduced
  (30ft -> 20ft). Heavy load: max Dex +1, check penalty -6, speed reduced, run x3.
